          "title": "Follows the hotter side",
          "desc": "Fan speed comes from the higher of the CPU and GPU sensor averages. The app shows which side it follows."
        },
        {
          "icon": "sliders-horizontal",
          "title": "Curve, Max or Apple auto",
          "desc": "Three presets and two sliders: where ramping starts and where full speed begins."
        },
        {
          "icon": "shield-check",
          "title": "Safety first",
          "desc": "Full speed if any sensor reaches 105 °C. Back to Apple auto if the service stops or loses the sensors."
        },
        {
          "icon": "chart-line",
          "title": "10-minute chart",
          "desc": "CPU and GPU temperatures and your curve on one screen. The menu bar shows the current temperature."
        },
        {
          "icon": "feather",
          "title": "Small footprint",
          "desc": "A small service in C controls the fans. The SwiftUI app only reads a status file and needs no privileges."
